Hey guys. I never posted here before, but I have been reading off an on
for a while now. I've been playing NetHack for a while, can't quite
remember when I started, but if memory serves, it was around the year
2000. Anyway, this is my second ascension, the first one was with a
Valkyrie. This time, it was a wizard. I've been trying to ascend a
wizard for quite a while now after many, many deaths.

The game began fairly normal until I entered Dlvl 3. I found a
-massive- sized ring shop with one amulet. I originally left the shop
as is, until I had ID scrolls. Then I came back to try to find a Ring
of Slow Digestion to use. Then I left the shop as is for now while I
went through the mines. Mine Town wasn't all that great, but I found
one magic lamp. Being conservative, I saved this lamp and used it as a
permanent light source for the time being. Got the luckstone at Mine's
End and I managed to find a polymorph on the way back up between that
and Mine Town. So I polymorphed my starting pet until It became a
Jabberwock. Awesome. Back in Mine Town, my Jabberwock had no trouble
annihalating every shopkeeper there. I deliberately kept it away from
the priest at first, however. Used the money I collected off the
shopkeepers to buy protection. Got magic bane there and some holy water
before I got out of the mines.

I cleared out the ring shop and tried to ID what rings I could at the
time, making a stash right there in the shop until later where I
transported all that stuff next to the quest area portal. I cleared out
Sokabon, managed to get a bag of holding (and the only one I would find
in the game). Unfortunately, the zoo there generated some winter wolves
which took out my stash of holy water, so I had to go back to mine town
to get some more later. Before I did that, I explored the levels all
the way down to the Medusa level. I was only level 13 at the time, so I
couldn't do the quest anyway. So I went back up to head back to Mine
Town so I could get more holy water that I needed. Perhaps I should
have done that sooner, but fortunately I took out a group of orcs, one
of which carried another Magic Lamp. I found out a little later that it
was blessed, so I used the first wish for a SDSM. My equipment at the
time was not complete and still had many vulnerabilities, and I didn't
like having to switch back and forth from my spells and my shield of
reflection that I picked up off an Aleax.

When I got to Mine Town, I ended up determining I had 2 holy waters
that I found. I suppose my original objective was a waste of time, but
not at this point. Since I picked up a couple more pets (and my
Jabberwock became a bloody gnomish wizard), I decided to go to the
level with the polymorph trap. Got myself an iron golem (which later
wielded Fire Brand), and a gargoyle.

The iron golem did pretty well, was fast, low AC, 236 HP's, and
seemingly pummeled everything in its wake. I ended up losing both pets
temporarily at the castle level when I went in the back way. I was
unaware that I losed the pets to the traps. I suppose I missed the
messages. After clearing the level, and grabbing the WoW, I headed down
to the Valley of the Dead. Lo and behold, my pets were there, except my
iron golem (my original pet too) was only peaceful. My scrolls of
taming had difficulty getting through his MR, so I left him alone after
a while until managed to get a Charm Monster spellbook which I promply
used to get my pet back. Unfortunately, that was a whole waste of time
as it didn't take long for my iron golem and my vampire (polymorphed
from the gargoyle) to get swallowed up by a Purple Worm on the same
level. So I charmed the worm instead, picked up my Fire Brand, and
headed downwards.

Gehennom was easy as cake at this point, taking out the bosses who
lingered there, and headed toward the bottom. Found another WoW along
the way, but I never did use it. I pretty much had everything I needed,
except for a few spells, which I used my castle wand for those (FoD and
Magic Mapping).

I got to the bottom, grabbed the amulet, and headed back up once more.
The Wizard of Yendor is a joke relative to a powerful wizard character
with the FoD spell. I slapped him to death with it 7 times. The other
death came from smacking him with a cockatrice corpse. That's always
fun. Anyway, got to the very top and headed into the Planes.

The Planes were extremely easy. The Plane of Air was the one I worried
about. When I played my Valkyrie, I didn't know all the tricks I could
have used, and had to use my Potions of Full Healing just to survive
enough to stumble upon the portal. My other Wizard had to quaff one,
but I got through that plane quickly with him. Anyway, the Plane of
Fire was easy and so was the Plane of Water. My last wizard that got
this far died on the Plane of Fire. I was engulfed by a fire elemental
and when I killed it, I landed in the middle of lava. I didn't know how
to get out of this, so that resulted in a fustrating death. Anyway,the
portal in the Plane of Water took a little while to find since it
moves, but I got through with little trouble.

I got to the Astral Plane and I was sweating this one. I was close to
ascending and didn't want to drop the ball here and die. I got lucky
with my Valkyrie (only other time I made it to the Astral as well),
since I picked the right spot to go the first time without having to
deal with many monsters, except Death which she promplty smacked him
down. Anyway, I started going to the far left, but Famine and some
priests were really jogging me up. I forgot the bless my Unicorn Horn,
but I managed to get through that after zapping a wand of death at
Famine and beat down the priest. I decided to turn back here and go up
the middle where Death was. Fortunately, Charm Monster came in handy
when the priests summoned insects. I tamed them to use as distractions
and as barriers. I had about 205 HP's max at the time and Death brought
it down to 161. Yikes. So I kept zapping him with the wand of
teleportation. I checked the altar there. Nope, no good. So I headed
back and to the left again. Again, no luck there. Finally, I went to
the last remaining altar and luck shined upon me today. I managed to
offer the amulet and ascend! Today is definitely a good day!

The only oddity out of all of this is that I died once somewhere with
an amulet of life saving before heading to the Planes. I have no idea
how that happened either. Again, not paying attention, I suppose.

